# help of a word defined more than once lists each definition as written, the program's or a used module's; the
# name used as a value is refused naming those definitions (card help-shows-overloads)
'use draw; help(save)'	"save(made: Picture, as file)\nsave(file: text)"
'f(x) := x\nf(x, y) := y\nhelp(f)'	"f(x)\nf(x, y)"
'f(a: int) := 1\nf(a: text) := 2\nhelp(f)'	"f(a: int)\nf(a: text)"
'f(x) := x; f(x, y) := y; g = f'	error	f is defined 2 times: f(x) and f(x, y); pass a lambda that calls the one you mean
'f(a: int) := 1; f(a: text) := 2; g = f'	error	f is defined 2 times: f(a: int) and f(a: text)
